      "point": "The robot TARS is a deliberate, friendlier echo of HAL from 2001, through an airlock joke, and was built and puppeteered on set rather than made purely with computer graphics.",
      "source": "https://www.nhpr.org/2014-11-07/christopher-nolan-on-blending-reality-into-fantasy-in-interstellar"
    },
    {
      "point": "Gargantua's accretion disk is deliberately 'anemic': roughly as hot as the Sun's surface, so it glows in visible light without the lethal radiation a real disk would give off. Physics, not just taste, shaped what the crew could look at.",
